2026-08-25T06:36:11Z info  argv: pr create --title Build strict: -ffp-contract=off on every target --body Brings RocketNet under the estate's standing floating-point policy (Glenn, 2026-08-24): network libraries require `-ffp-contract=off`. Same landing as netcode #179, reliable #54 and yojimbo #333 — with flow, this completes the family of six.\n\n- `build/CMakeLists.txt` sets `-ffp-contract=off` (GCC/Clang) / `/fp:precise` (MSVC) globally, so the library, the C++ tests and the C examples all build with it; CI builds through this file via `make`.\n- New `BUILDING.md` documents the build and states the consumer requirement, in the family's standard shape.\n\nRocketNet's floats are connection config and stats (RTT, jitter, packet loss, bandwidth), so no consumer flag is needed for correct wire bytes today — this is the family floor. Contraction is architecture-dependent (FMA in the aarch64 baseline, absent from x86-64), so unflagged float arithmetic near a wire diverges bit-wise between architectures.\n\nVerified locally on macOS: clean `make`, all 7 entries in `compile_commands.json` carry the flag, `./dist/test` exits 0 ("All tests passed").\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
